Hi [~accountid:712020:60da7793-200e-4a92-a78d-1705c6e5cdf8] - thanks for looping me in on this. 

In short, it looks like {color:#36b37e}*we can proceed with the temporary setup*{color} (i.e., using the Google Form) +*_provided that_*+ we include some disclaimer language in the form. I include further details below.

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
*Issue 1: Does the agreement with Circle K cover this?*
{panel}

In short, {color:#36b37e}*yes*{color} - The agreement covers scenarios where Bolt shares the names and phone numbers and drivers with Circle K ✅ 

However, this conclusion is based on the assumptions that: (a) this agreement is still in force; and (b) we are only talking about transfers between Bolt’s and Circle K’s _Lithuanian_ entities - *please confirm if either of these do not apply* (?) 

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
*Issue 2: Can we use the temporary setup of the Google Form?*
{panel}

In short, {color:#36b37e}*yes*{color} - This approach is much more proportionate than sending the names and phone numbers of _all_ newly registered drivers (which  would not recommend for a few reasons) ✅ 

The only notable risk here is ensuring that drivers are fully *clear on what the form is for and how their data will be shared* with Circle K. This is because: (i) are required to inform drivers about this under applicable law; and (ii) being transparent about this will minimise the risk of driver complaints / questions. To address this, we should include the following disclaimer language in the form, and *_only_* share the details of drivers who have provided their details via the form:

{quote}“_By providing your contact information via this form, Bolt will share it with Circle K Lietuva, UAB (and its affiliated companies) based on Bolt’s legitimate interest in facilitating your participation in the Bolt Rewards Programme. For more information on how your personal data is processed, please see our privacy notice available at_ [+_https://bolt.eu/lt-lt/privacy/privacy-for-drivers/?category=rides_+|https://bolt.eu/lt-lt/privacy/privacy-for-drivers/?category=rides]”{quote}

I would be grateful if you could *please share a copy of the Google Form with me before it goes live*, so that I can double-check and green-light it 🙏  

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
*Issue 3: Anything else to flag?*
{panel}

We should be doing this already, but just to flag for completeness - Given that this setup involves marketing Circle K’s services to Bolt drivers, where we are sending such comms to drivers via *_direct / targeted_* means (e.g., email, text message, push notifications), we should only be doing this for drivers that have opt-in consented to receiving such comms (i.e., drivers who have selected ‘Partner Offers’ in the consents section of their profile)💡 

* Where we are promoting Circle K’s discounts via *_general / untargeted_* means (e.g., posting a link to the Google Form on general Bolt Rewards pages), we do not need to rely on opt-in driver consent to do so.

If you have any questions then let me know. I will otherwise await a copy of the Google Form 🙂

