As per our previous conversation you pointed out this:

{color:#6554c0}_Sorry for the delay on this, but I needed to go through S.L. 499.68 very carefully in order to make sure there was no major blockers._{color}

{color:#6554c0}_This topic requires a few considerations._{color}

{color:#6554c0}_In your message you write that “these are free standing stands that Riders can use in order to book Bolt rides through kiosks with no app required”._{color}

{color:#6554c0}_So, first, we need to check if this is possible under S.L. 499.68._{color}

{color:#6554c0}_Reg 15(2) states that Light passenger transport services may only be sold or booked from authorised  commercial  premises,  from  the operator’s offices or operating centre, online, by web application, by telephone, by mail or through authorised intermediaries._{color}

{color:#6554c0}_So, the “no app required” part is generally possible._{color}

{color:#6554c0}_As you know, Bolt is licensed as an "intermediary booking service platform", which means a “platform whereby light passenger transport services may be booked by customers from operators of light passenger transport services through an intermediary holding an authorisation for such purpose from the Authority”._{color}

{color:#6554c0}_My view is that, as long as the Kiosks are integrated into Bolt’s system, the same obligations apply — nothing in the law requires the booking platform to be accessed only by an app._{color}

{color:#6554c0}_However, I would like to know how are you planning to do roll this out with no-app? Wouldn’t the Kiosk correspond to a device that has an app integrated where Users could login (in the case they already have an account with Bolt) or register (in case they don’t have a pre-existing account)?_{color}

{color:#6554c0}_Please note that, if the no-app premise maintains, we will need to have specific T&C’s._{color}

{color:#6554c0}_From a legal and regulatory perspective under S.L. 499.68, I don’t think there are blockers to launching Kiosks in Malta, provided:_{color}

* {color:#6554c0}_Bookings through Kiosks are processed within Bolt’s registered booking platform;_{color}
* {color:#6554c0}_Only licensed LPTS operators are used;_{color}
* {color:#6554c0}_Fare transparency and consumer information requirements are respected (Cap. 378 Consumer Affairs Act and the Omnibus Directive (EU 2019/2161) - the Kiosk interface must provide the same consumer rights information as the app);_{color}
* {color:#6554c0}_Data handling complies with GDPR._{color}

{color:#6554c0}*_However, I would advise to consult/notify Transport Malta before rollout, to confirm that the Kiosk channel is covered under Bolt’s existing booking platform registration._* {color}{color:#36b37e}_- Sure I will check with TM about this._ {color}

{color:#6554c0}_Regarding the specific questions asked:_{color}

{color:#6554c0}_Do you believe we would need a permit in order to install physical infrastructure?_ {color}

{color:#6554c0}_It depends on where this infrastructure will be installed. If it is in a public space (bus stations, council land, etc), authorisation/licence will most probably be required._{color}

{color:#6554c0}_If Kiosks are to be installed inside private commercial premises, landlord consent suffices._ {color}{color:#36b37e}_- Noted, majority are in a Private Space, and then a contract with the supplier would be needed._{color}

{color:#6554c0}_Do you think we would need a contract to be put in place?_ {color}{color:#36b37e}_- Yes_{color}

{color:#6554c0}_If kiosks are placed on third-party property (airport, shopping mall, event venue, hotel), Bolt will need a placement/use contract with the property owner._ {color}{color:#36b37e}_- Agreed_{color}

{color:#6554c0}_If placed in public space, Bolt would need a concession/authorisation agreement with the relevant public authority._{color}

{color:#6554c0}_Is there any Data privacy issues that we need to be aware of if we are collecting User info?_ {color}{color:#36b37e}_- I believe this was done from Privacy perspective._{color}

{color:#6554c0}_Do you think that we will face any blockers to launch this?_ {color}

{color:#6554c0}_No blockers under S.L. 499.68: A kiosk can be another “electronic platform” for booking, provided all bookings are routed through Bolt’s registered platform and only licensed operators are dispatched._{color}
{color:#6554c0}_Main risks are planning/permit approval, contracts for location, and GDPR compliance._{color}
{color:#6554c0}_Bolt should also notify/consult Transport Malta before rollout — not legally mandated but advisable for regulatory goodwill._ {color}{color:#36b37e}_- Agreed._{color}

{color:#6554c0}_Have you approached any entity (public or private) regarding the installation of kiosks? -_ {color}{color:#36b37e}_Yes, we have several locations:_ {color}


* {color:#36b37e}_Mercury (Shopping Centre) - Confirmed (Cost: 2% of Rides) x1_{color}
* {color:#36b37e}_Mater Dei (Hospital) - Confirmed (Cost: Free) x2_{color}
* {color:#36b37e}_Numero UNO (Venue) - TBC x1_{color}
* {color:#36b37e}_Gianpula (Venue) - TBC x1_{color}


So as a way forward

*  I will contact Transport Malta
* Would you be able to guide me about contract creation, I believe that Merve, is already working one something in relation to other countries.

Thank you!

